Description: Fix value_or template deduction failure in profile_network_context_service
 In C++23 with system libc++, value_or({}) on std::optional<std::vector<uint8_t>>
 fails template argument deduction because {} cannot be inferred as the value type.
 Replace with explicit conditional to avoid the deduction issue.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-04-08

diff --git a/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc b/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
index d0bb264..6073ec7 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
@@ -1287,7 +1287,8 @@ std::vector<uint8_t>
 ProfileNetworkContextService::GetEncryptedCachePrimaryKey() {
   std::string encoded_encrypted_primary_key = profile_->GetPrefs()->GetString(
       enterprise_connectors::kEncryptedCachePrimaryKey);
-  return base::Base64Decode(encoded_encrypted_primary_key).value_or({});
+  auto decoded = base::Base64Decode(encoded_encrypted_primary_key);
+  return decoded ? std::move(*decoded) : std::vector<uint8_t>{};
 }

 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENTERPRISE_CACHE_ENCRYPTION)
